[{"id":"F1","path":"README.md","status":"modified","additions":5,"deletions":0,"language":"markdown","hunks":[{"id":"F1.H1","header":"@@ -1636,6 +1636,11 @@ Two assembly-level attributes exist to help with mixing in your own custom forma","oldStart":1636,"newStart":1636,"lines":[{"t":"ctx","o":1636,"n":1636,"s":""},{"t":"ctx","o":1637,"n":1637,"s":"Learn more about using a mix of your own custom formatters and automatically generated ones in [the Analyzer section](#analyzer)."},{"t":"ctx","o":1638,"n":1638,"s":""},{"t":"add","n":1639,"s":"### Generic types from referenced assemblies"},{"t":"add","n":1640,"s":""},{"t":"add","n":1641,"s":"Closed generic types defined in a referenced assembly (for example, `Item<int>` where `Item<T>` is defined in another project or NuGet package) can be used as members of your `[MessagePackObject]` types, including generic value types and record structs."},{"t":"add","n":1642,"s":"Diagnostics about the members of such a type are reported by the assembly that defines it rather than by the consuming project, so any problem must be fixed there."},{"t":"add","n":1643,"s":""},{"t":"ctx","o":1639,"n":1644,"s":"### MagicOnion"},{"t":"ctx","o":1640,"n":1645,"s":""},{"t":"ctx","o":1641,"n":1646,"s":"[MagicOnion](https://github.com/Cysharp/MagicOnion) is a code-first gRPC framework based on grpc-dotnet and MessagePack. gRPC usually communicates with Protocol Buffers using IDL. But MagicOnion uses MessagePack for C# and does not need IDL. When communicating C# to C#, schemaless (or rather C# classes as schema) is better than using IDL."}],"unitId":"U5"}]},{"id":"F2","path":"doc/analyzers/MsgPack004.md","status":"modified","additions":5,"deletions":0,"language":"markdown","hunks":[{"id":"F2.H1","header":"@@ -45,3 +45,8 @@ public class C {","oldStart":45,"newStart":45,"lines":[{"t":"ctx","o":45,"n":45,"s":"    public int B { get; set; }"},{"t":"ctx","o":46,"n":46,"s":"}"},{"t":"ctx","o":47,"n":47,"s":"```"},{"t":"add","n":48,"s":""},{"t":"add","n"